  provenance: 'Bells: USN convention (1/3, 2/3, standard, full = 4/3 standard, flank
    = maximum); standard 15 kn AUTHORED; flank = the Engine Room''s top speed.

    Astern
    bells: 1/3, 2/3, 0.85, 1.0 of maximum astern revolutions (AUTHORED).

    Course
    hold: Kp 2, Kd 20 deg/(deg/s), at most 20 deg of rudder (AUTHORED, tuned on this
    hull: a 90 deg course change settles to 1 deg without overshoot in 183 / 109
    / 82 s at 10 / 20 / 30 kn).

    Speed hold: steady-revolution feed-forward plus
    Kp 0.05 rev/s per kn, Ki 0.001 (AUTHORED).

    Routes: plan turns at 15 deg
    (USN standard rudder), line-of-sight look-ahead 2 ship lengths (AUTHORED).'
